<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Congress Poland</h1><p class="st-meta">1815 CE – 1915 CE · capital Warsaw</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Kingdom of Poland created at Vienna under the Russian tsar, scene of two great uprisings and of Poland's industrial revolution.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> in 1815 turned most of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-warsaw">Duchy of Warsaw</a> into a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1916-1918">Kingdom of Poland</a> joined to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> by personal union, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Tsar Alexander I</a> as king. It received a liberal constitution, its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>, army, currency and administration, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In practice the tsar's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-konstantin-pavlovich-of-russia">Grand Duke Constantine</a> commanded the army and disregarded the constitution. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/november-uprising">November Uprising</a> of 1830 was crushed, and Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-paskevich">Ivan Paskevich</a> governed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> for decades. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/january-uprising">January Uprising</a> of 1863 the kingdom lost its remaining autonomy and was renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> Land, with Russian imposed in schools. At the same time <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodz">Lodz</a> grew into a great textile city.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> German and Austro-Hungarian armies drove the Russians out in 1915. The occupiers proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1916-1918">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1916-1918), and its lands became the core of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-polish-republic">Second Polish Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/congress-poland.jpg" alt="Congress Poland" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: Blank_map_of_Europe.svg: maix¿? derivative work: Alphathon /'æɫfə.θɒn/ (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congress_Poland_1815.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1815 CE – 1915 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Warsaw</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alexander I, Grand Duke Constantine, Ivan Paskevich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Poland</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Poland (1815-1915), Vistula Land, Russian Poland</dd></dl></aside></div>
